---
#2766: a bounded generic type declared in one unit; its statics take hidden
comparators that a caller in another unit builds, concretely and from a rigid
type parameter of its own.
---
commons demo.sorted

uses bynk.list

type Sorted[T: Ord] = { items: List[T] }

fn Sorted.fromList(xs: List[T]) -> Sorted[T] { Sorted { items: sort(xs) } }

fn Sorted.empty() -> Sorted[T] { Sorted { items: [] } }
